[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:It Could be Worse]
[00:14.96]Had the writer's money been stolen?
[00:20.58]I entered the hotel manager's office and sat down.
[00:27.31]I had just lost ￡50 and I felt very upset.
[00:35.67]'I left the money in my room,' I said,'and it's not there now.'
[00:43.81]The manager was sympathetic, but he could do nothing.
[00:50.25]'Everyone's losing money these days,' he said.
[00:54.94]He started to complain about this wicked world but was interrupted by a knock at the door.
[01:04.04]A girl came in and put an envelope on his desk.
[01:09.37]It contained ￡50.
[01:14.03]'I found this outside this gentleman's room,' she said.
[01:20.01]'Well,' I said to the manager,'there is still some honesty in this world!'
